WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.600
You had, in athletics, LSU went along with the Army and they had the ASTP [Army Specialized Training Program] program.

2
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.540
They had no contact with the . . . direct contact with the students.

3
00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:15.480
They might after hours, you know.

4
00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:19.400
But during hours they had no contact at all with students.

5
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:24.080
Nor could they participate in intercollegiate athletics.

6
00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:34.120
Now, the schools affiliated with the Navy, their V-12 program, like Tulane and Southwestern, they went to the same classes as civilians went to.

7
00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:40.840
They would not live in the same dormitory, but they would participate in social activities with the civilian students.

8
00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:45.920
They’d go to class with them and they could participate in football and so on and so forth.

9
00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:53.840
So as a consequence, schools like LSU suffered from an athletics standpoint.

10
00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:59.000
One year we had a bad record, I forgot what it was, seven [wins] four [losses], something like that.

11
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.160
It was not a good record.

12
00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:00.920
In football?

13
00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:02.300
In football.

14
00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:10.620
And we still got invited to the [1944] Orange Bowl because they figured we were one of the best civilian teams around.

15
00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:16.260
And played Texas A&amp;M, which is one of the best civilian teams around.

16
00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:20.400
We defeated Texas A&amp;M although we’d lost to them during the regular season.

17
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:21.180
But it was bad.

18
00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:26.240
For example, Alabama that year had canceled its football season.

19
00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:28.260
They couldn’t field a good team.

20
00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:31.920
To find schools to play, we played Georgia twice in one year.

21
00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:34.353
Who?

22
00:01:34.353 --> 00:01:39.220
Georgia.

23
00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:39.420
University of Georgia.

24
00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:39.420
Oh, okay.

25
00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:39.420
Twice?

26
00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:39.420
Twice.

27
00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:40.360
They were army schools.

28
00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:47.940
So you had a sort of dual thing there and there was . . . It was just entirely different.

29
00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:50.768
Now, at LSU all they did was come in and fuss about the tiger [LSU mascot,

30
00:01:50.768 --> 00:01:54.960
Mike] making too much noise, which irked the rest of us.

31
00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:56.660
I don’t get that.

32
00:01:56.660 --> 00:02:01.480
Well, the tiger cage . . . They moved us out of the North Stadium [dorms], moved them in.

33
00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:06.180
And the thing they complain about is not being able to sleep because of the tiger’s roar.

34
00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:08.960
Well, I put up with it before and it didn’t bother me. [laughing]
